---
layout: base.njk
---
{#
  Layout for input_custom_post/ — block posts, hand-written OR exported by the
  page builder (page_builder_app_v2). Both kinds are the same thing: YAML front
  matter plus a BODY fragment.

  Sits between base.njk and that fragment. base.njk supplies <!DOCTYPE>, the
  <head>, nav.njk and footer.njk; this file adds the furniture every notebook
  post carries — the date/title/back-link header and the closing date rule +
  "← NOTEBOOK FRONT PAGE" link, both from post_chrome.njk — so a body never
  carries any of it. eleventy.config.js stops the build if one carries the
  ending, because this file would add a second.

  WHY THIS IS NOT post.njk
  post.njk wraps everything in `.post-container > .prose`, which is correct for
  markdown and wrong for blocks: a full-bleed hero cannot escape a max-width
  column. Here {{ content }} is emitted at FULL WIDTH and each block brings its
  own container. That is the one real difference; the header and the ending
  are the same macros post.njk uses, so the two page kinds cannot drift apart.

  eleventy_njk/_builder_shell.njk renders the same header and ending around a
  {{CONTENT}} token, in the same order as below, for the page builder's
  preview. Reorder one, reorder the other.

  FRONT MATTER THIS LAYOUT READS
    header: false   omit the date/title/back-link header, for a page that opens
                    on its own hero and carries its own title and back link.
                    The page builder writes it for exactly those pages.
    outline: true   add the "On this page" panel, built from the h2/h3 in the
                    body. Off by default: addAnchors rewrites every heading in
                    the fragment, including ones inside a hero, which is rarely
                    what a block page wants.
  Everything else (title, date, tags, image, description, navScroll,
  customJsonLd) is read by base.njk, not here.
#}
{% from "post_chrome.njk" import postHeaderBlock, postEnding %}
{% set dateIso = date | isoStamp %}
{% set dateHuman = date | readableDate %}

{% if outline %}
{% set body = content | addAnchors %}
{% set toclist = body | toc %}
{% else %}
{% set body = content %}
{% set toclist = "" %}
{% endif %}

{% if toclist %}
{# No-JS article outline: hidden checkbox drives the toggle. Same markup as post.njk. #}
<input type="checkbox" id="article-outline-toggle" class="article-outline-toggle">
<aside class="article-outline-panel">
    <p class="article-outline-heading">On this page</p>
    {{ toclist | safe }}
</aside>
<label for="article-outline-toggle" class="article-outline-btn" title="Toggle outline" aria-label="Toggle outline">
    <span class="article-outline-icon-open" aria-hidden="true">E</span>
    <span class="article-outline-icon-close" aria-hidden="true">X</span>
</label>
{% endif %}

{% if header != false %}
{{ postHeaderBlock(title, dateIso, dateHuman) }}
{% endif %}

{# FULL WIDTH on purpose — see the note at the top. Each block supplies its own
   container: .post-container for a text column, nothing for a full-bleed one. #}
{{ body | safe }}

{{ postEnding(dateIso, dateHuman) }}
